      "        \u001b[0m\u001b[34;1m\"reasoning\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"Thinking Process:\\n\\n1.  **Deconstruct the topic:** Protein-protein interactions (PPIs).\\n    *   Keywords: Proteins, bind, interact, shape, lock, key, complex, signal, life, molecular, dance, embrace, function.\\n    *   Concepts: Two proteins coming together, specific binding, conformational changes, biological function, cellular machinery.\\n\\n2.  **Brainstorm imagery and metaphors:**\\n    *   Lock and key (classic, but maybe cliché? Good for haiku though).\\n    *   Dance (elegant, movement).\\n    *   Handshake (greeting, connection).\\n    *   Puzzle pieces fitting.\\n    *   Molecular embrace.\\n\\n3.  **Drafting - Attempt 1 (Focus on structure 5-7-5):**\\n    *   *Line 1:* Two proteins meet now (5 syllables).\\n    *   *Line 2:* Binding tight like lock and key (7 syllables).\\n    *   *Line 3:* Life flows through the cell (5 syllables).\\n    *   *Critique:* A bit generic. \\\"Lock and key\\\" is overused. \\\"Life flows\\\" is vague.\\n\\n4.  **Drafting - Attempt 2 (Focus on imagery):**\\n    *   *Line 1:* Shapes find perfect fit (5 syllables).\\n    *   *Line 2:* A molecular embrace (7 syllables).\\n    *   *Line 3:* Signals start to flow (5 syllables).\\n    *   *Critique:* Better. \\\"Shapes find perfect fit\\\" is good. \\\"Molecular embrace\\\" is nice. \\\"Signals start to flow\\\" explains the function. Syllable count: Shapes find per-fect fit (5). A mol-e-cu-lar em-brace (7). Sig-nals start to flow (5). This works.\\n\\n5.  **Drafting - Attempt 3 (More poetic/scientific blend):**\\n    *   *Line 1:* Folds lock, surfaces kiss (5 syllables).\\n    *   *Line 2:* Complex forms, signals ignite (7 syllables).\\n    *   *Line 3:* Life's machinery turns (5 syllables).\\n    *   *Critique:* \\\"Folds lock\\\" is a bit awkward. \\\"Surfaces kiss\\\" is personification, good. \\\"Complex forms\\\" is accurate. \\\"Signals ignite\\\" is strong. \\\"Life's machinery turns\\\" is a good closing. Syllables: Folds lock, sur-faces kiss (6? No. Folds lock, sur-faces kiss. Folds(1) lock(1), sur(1)fa(1)ces(1) kiss(1) = 6 syllables. Fail.)\\n    *   *Fix Line 1:* Folds lock, soft surfaces kiss (6? Folds lock, soft sur-faces kiss = 7. Too long.)\\n    *   *Fix Line 1:* Shapes lock, surfaces kiss (5). Good.\\n    *   *Result:* Shapes lock, surfaces kiss / Complex forms, signals ignite / Life's machinery turns.\\n    *   *Critique:* \\\"Shapes lock\\\" is okay. \\\"Surfaces kiss\\\" is good. \\\"Complex forms\\\" is good. \\\"Signals ignite\\\" is good. \\\"Life's machinery turns\\\" is good. This is strong.\\n\\n6.  **Final Polish (Selecting the best version):**\\n    *   *Option A:* Shapes find perfect fit / A molecular embrace / Signals start to flow.\\n    *   *Option B:* Shapes lock, surfaces kiss / Complex forms, signals ignite / Life's machinery turns.\\n    *   *Comparison:* Option B has more dynamic verbs (\\\"lock\\\", \\\"kiss\\\", \\\"ignite\\\", \\\"turns\\\"). It feels more active. \\\"Molecular embrace\\\" in Option A is nice but \\\"surfaces kiss\\\" is more tactile. \\\"Signals ignite\\\" vs \\\"Signals start to flow\\\". \\\"Ignite\\\" implies the trigger aspect of PPIs well.\\n    *   *Decision:* Option B is slightly better poetically.\\n    *   *Syllable Check on Option B:*\\n        *   Shapes lock, sur-faces kiss (5).\\n        *   Com-plex forms, sig-nals ig-nite (7).\\n        *   Life's ma-chin-ery turns (5).\\n        *   Perfect.\\n\\n7.  **Output Generation:**\\n    Shapes lock, surfaces kiss,\\n    Complex forms, signals ignite,\\n    Life's machinery turns.\\n\\n    *Wait, let me double check \\\"surfaces\\\".*\\n    Sur-faces. Two syllables.\\n    Shapes lock, sur-faces kiss.\\n    Shapes(1) lock(1), sur(1)fa(1)ces(1) kiss(1).\\n    Total: 5. Correct.\\n\\n    *Double check \\\"complex\\\".*\\n    Com-plex. Two syllables.\\n    Com-plex forms, sig-nals ig-nite.\\n    Com(1)plex(1) forms(1), sig(1)nals(1) ig(1)nite(1).\\n    Total: 7. Correct.\\n\\n    *Double check \\\"machinery\\\".*\\n    Ma-chin-ery. Three syllables.\\n    Life's ma-chin-ery turns.\\n    Life's(1) ma(1)chin(1)ery(1) turns(1).\\n    Total: 5. Correct.\\n\\n    Result is solid.\\n\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\n",
